- By setting this sysctl to a value larger than any object we intend to allocate (e.g., `"64"`), we ensure that small allocations are served from the global pool rather than a per‑thread cache.
- Consequently, even if an attacker writes past a buffer’s end, there is no hidden tcache entry that can be abused; all freed chunks are tracked globally and cannot be reused before being returned safely.
